  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>The US military completed a seventh consecutive night of airstrikes against Iranian targets overnight July 17–18, with CENTCOM confirming strikes on surveillance infrastructure, military logistics nodes, underground weapons storage, and coastal maritime capabilities. Iran answered each wave in kind: Kuwait's air defense network issued seven separate threat warnings across twelve hours into Saturday morning, Jordan's batteries intercepted 10 Iranian ballistic missiles and cruise missiles over Jordanian territory, and Bahrain activated public shelter sirens for a third night running. Both sides conducted confirmed offensive operations within the same 24-hour window across multiple theaters for the fifth consecutive day.
      → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>An IRGC official and military adviser to Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei issued a public warning through semi-official Iranian media on Saturday morning that Iran would enter full-scale offensive operations against US forces and US-allied regional targets if airstrikes persisted for another two to three days. No corresponding diplomatic signal from Washington acknowledged the warning or offered terms.
      → moved <span class="cite">F8</span></p>

      <p>An Oman-hosted session on July 11 addressed Hormuz maritime security mechanics in general terms but produced no documented halt in hostilities from either side, and the Strait remained at approximately 10 commercial transits per day against a pre-crisis baseline of 88; 444 commercial vessels are reported at anchor or drifting in adjacent waters, with war-risk insurance now priced at eight times pre-conflict levels and six P&amp;I clubs having withdrawn cover entirely.
      → supports <span class="cite">F9</span>; supports <span class="cite">F11</span>; <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Israel's Knesset voted 62-0 to dissolve itself in the early hours of July 17, completing the 25th Knesset's full four-year legal mandate — the first time since 1988 that an Israeli parliament ran to the end of its term without interruption. All 62 votes in favor came from coalition members; opposition lawmakers boycotted the session. In a final legislative session running overnight, the coalition passed judicial overhaul provisions stripping the attorney-general of supervisory powers, Haredi military draft-exemption legislation, and expanded government oversight of media outlets. Netanyahu voted personally in favor of dissolution. Elections are now locked at October 27, 2026.
      → moved <span class="cite">F6</span>; moved <span class="cite">F7</span></p>

      <p>State funeral processions for assassinated Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei continued in Tehran and other Iranian cities on July 17–18, the fifth and sixth days of an official mourning period, drawing tens of thousands of organized mourners. New Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei — formally appointed by the Assembly of Experts on March 8 — has not been seen or heard from publicly since his appointment; US Secretary of Defense Pete Hegseth stated in March that Mojtaba had been wounded and likely disfigured in the same strike that killed his father. Qatari mediators stated publicly that the next US-Iran technical session would be organized after the conclusion of the funeral events, providing no specific date.
      → moved <span class="cite">F12</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

