      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (25%):</strong> Both governments have sustained the July 8–18 operational tempo without crossing the catastrophic thresholds coded in F8 (22%) or F10 (20%); attritional exchange at roughly current intensity without dramatic shift remains structurally possible.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (10%):</strong> A new formal ceasefire framework (F9, 30%) is the sole active de-escalation pathway, but seven consecutive US strike nights, the IRGC full-scale operations threat, and no confirmed mediator session with named delegations reduce the probability of a sustained halt well below F9's nominal 14-day window probability alone.</p>
